  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653. We know scvi_n200 > pca_n2000 (0.520 vs 0.485 singleprofile) and multiprofile >> singleprofile (0.65+ vs 0.52), but we have no data on scgpt in the multiprofile setting. Image-only is very weak (0.208), making multimodal gains uncertain. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder in the multiprofile + transformer pipeline? This is a clean single-variable comparison against config_006, isolating encoder quality. Why this is best: With 4 experiments left, we need to determine whether the RNA encoder is the bottleneck before investing budget in multimodal fusion. If scgpt improves on 0.653, it gives a stronger baseline for subsequent multimodal tests; if not, we confirm scvi_n200 is optimal and can focus remaining experiments on whether multimodal (especially with ViT-L) adds value over the RNA-only ceiling."
